    "University Library – Hokkaido University\nSkip to content\nAs one of Japan’s leading research libraries, the Hokkaido University libraries hold approximately 3.70 million books and journals, including a unique collection of materials focused on the northern region. To raise the standard of academic communication, we continue to increase our electronic collection and develop our institutional repository. With a seating capacity of over 1,500, our libraries continue to play a vital role as places of learning.\nOfficial Website\nLibrary Hours\nNote:\nLibrary hours vary depending on the time of year. Please check\nthe library’s website\nfor further information.\nName of Rooms\nMonday–Friday\nWeekends & Holidays\nOpen-stack reading rooms\n8:00–22:00\n9:00–19:00\nStack rooms\n9:00–20:00\n9:00–18:30\nGroup study rooms (Central Library)\n8:30–21:30\n9:00–18:30\nIndividual study booth (Central Library)\n8:30–22:00\n9:00–19:00\nGroup study rooms (North Library)\n8:00–21:30\n9:00–18:30\nMultimedia room (North Library)\n8:00–21:30\n9:00–19:00\nClosed\nJune 7-8 (North Library only), August 13-15 (North Library Only), August 20-21 (Central Library Only), September 13-15, December 27-January 4, January 17-18\nCollection by Branch\nBranch\nJapanese Books\nForeign Books\nTotal Books\nJournals\nCentral Library\n1,037,189\n886,439\n1,923,628\n36,288\n88North Library\n270,939\n118,052\n388,991\n1,616\nSubtotal\n1,308,128\n1,004,491\n2,312,619\n37,904\nBranch\nJapanese Books\nForeign Books\nTotal Books\nJournals\nCreative Research Institution\n19\n3\n22\n4\nInstitute for the Advancement of Higher Education\n2,583\n647\n3,230\n151\nInstitute for International Collaboration\n1\n0\n1\n3\nInstitute for the Advancement of Graduate Education\n112\n10\n122\n1\nLetters\n104,261\n45,878\n150,139\n2,678\nLaw\n7,696\n1,709\n9,405\n899\nInformation Science and Technology*\n13,768\n17,016\n30,784\n849\nFisheries Sciences\n73,290\n54,605\n127,895\n5,460\nEnvironmental Science/Environmental Earth